  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the UI components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the UI components and am starting with the Navbar. I\'ve decided on the branding: a \"NEURAL NEXUS\" logo with a sleek white square icon containing a black square. The Navbar will feature navigation tabs for Marketplace, Community, Directory, and News Channel, along with a search function.\n\n\n**Refining the Navbar**\n\nI\'ve added a global search bar to the navbar, allowing users to search across all sections. The \"Access Vault\" button will display purchased assets, and I\'m including a \"Sell/List Asset\" button. Status indicators are also being added, initially a \"System Status: Optimal\" indicator with a green dot.\n\n\n**Developing Asset Details**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the asset presentation. I\'m structuring a compelling display: a bold, uppercase category badge, the price clearly marked, and a concise title and tagline. Key metrics like downloads, ratings, and an efficiency score, highlighted in green if appropriate, will be readily visible. Plus, a \"View Details\" button and a \"Buy / Access\" quick trigger for immediate action.\n\\n\\n\nI\'ve moved on to the Asset Detail & Sandbox Modal, and I\'m fleshing out its core functionality. I\'m including complete technical specs (framework, base model, parameters, format, context window). I\'m also planning a system prompt preview and code view. Crucially, I\'m integrating an interactive demo playground. Users will be able to test asset outputs with a sample input, or simulate API executions. The final element is a \"Checkout & Acquire\" button. This will lead to the checkout modal.\nI\'m building a Checkout Gateway Modal now. I\'m focusing on secure payment options, allowing for credit card and cryptocurrency (USDT / Solana / ETH). The modal will present a clear price breakdown, including the asset price, a license fee of $0, and instant vault delivery. I\'m including the generation of an instant license key. Lastly, I\'ll include a download link and API key activation link.\n\n\n**Building the Community Hub**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Community Hub, calling it \"Collective Brain,\" and designing the interface. I\'m focusing on post filters, like \"Model Review\" and \"Support Request\". Posts will show author info, upvotes, and replies, plus a button to generate enhancement tips. A modal will facilitate new post submissions, including title, model details, and code.\n\n**Creating the Global Directory**\n\nI\'m starting the Global AI Index, the directory, which I\'ve titled the \"Global AI Index.\" I\'ve sorted categories to include things like Text LLMs, Frameworks, and Code. I\'m focusing on searchability, with a search bar and filter for type, such as open source versus proprietary.\n\n\n**Designing the News Channel**\n\nI\'m now designing the \"Daily AI Intelligence\" News Channel. I\'m imagining a ticker banner with live audio broadcasts and category filters like Hardware News and Model Release. Each news article will display an impact badge, timestamp, and source, with a full article accessible via a drawer or modal. Users will have bookmarking capabilities and be able to submit news tips via a dedicated modal. I\'ve also shifted my focus to the global directory, and decided to show cards with official external links, context window specs, parameters count, pricing info, ratings, and tags.\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing the Access Vault Modal, and I\'ll display the user\'s acquired AI models, workflows, license keys, API endpoints, and download links. I\'m following that up with a List New Asset Modal, which will enable users to list their own AI model, workflow, or chatbot for sale or free on Neural Nexus.\nI\'m rounding things out with a Footer component, which will include Copyright and System Status information. The footer will also display \"Market Volatility: Low\", and \"Verified Builders: 1,429\".\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 97006617
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
